The `handleAttackSelection()` method selects a random attack number between 1 and 2 and prints it to the console. The `handleConnectionStateChange(int newState)` method handles connection state changes by checking if the connection has been established, allowing the game character to use an attack if the cooldown period has expired, or waiting for the cooldown period to expire if it is still active.

The `isCooldownActive` and `lastAttackTime` variables are used to keep track of the current state of the cooldown period. The `handleAttackSelection()` method sets `isCooldownActive` to true when an attack is selected, and sets `lastAttackTime` to the current time in milliseconds. The `handleConnectionStateChange(int newState)` method checks if the connection has been established, allows the game character to use an attack if the cooldown period has expired, or waits for the cooldown period to expire if it is still active.

```c#
using System;

public class CustomRandomGenerator
{
    private readonly Random _random;
    private readonly bool _seeded;
    private readonly int? _seed;

    public CustomRandomGenerator(bool seeded, int? seed)
    {
        _seeded = seeded;
        _seed = seed;
        if (_seeded)
        {
            UnityEngine.Random.Seed(_seed);
        }
        _random = new Random();
    }

    public float CustomRange(float min, float max, bool isExclusive, int? seed)
    {
        // Validate input parameters
        if (min > max)
            throw new ArgumentException("Min value must be less than or equal to max value");
        if (!isExclusive && min == max)
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid range specified, cannot generate a random value within the same value");
        if (seed.HasValue && !_seeded)
            throw new InvalidOperationException("Seed is not applicable when seeding is disabled");

        // Generate random value based on specified range and seed
        float value = _random.NextDouble() * (max - min) + min;
        if (!isExclusive && value == max)
            value = max - 1e-6f;
        return value;
    }

    public int CustomRange(int min, int max, bool isExclusive, int? seed)
    {
        // Validate input parameters
        if (min > max)
            throw new ArgumentException("Min value must be less than or equal to max value");
        if (!isExclusive && min == max)
            throw new ArgumentException("Invalid range specified, cannot generate a random value within the same value");
        if (seed.HasValue && !_seeded)
            throw new InvalidOperationException("Seed is not applicable when seeding is disabled");

        // Generate random value based on specified range and seed
        int value = _random.Next(max - min + 1) + min;
        if (!isExclusive && value == max)
            value--;
        return value;
    }

    public override string ToString()
    {
        // Return a string representation of the random generator, including the range and seed if applicable
        var builder = new StringBuilder();
        builder.AppendLine($"CustomRandomGenerator: Seeded = {_seeded}");
        if (_seed.HasValue)
            builder.AppendLine($"Seed = {_seed.ToString()}");
        builder.AppendLine($"Range = [{min}, {max}]");
        return builder.ToString();
    }
}
```
This implementation provides a class that can generate random values within a specified range, both inclusively and exclusively, for both floating-point and integer types. The class also supports seeded and unseeded random number generation, with the option to provide a custom seed value. Additionally, it includes error handling for invalid input parameters and seeding, as well as mechanisms for managing resources efficiently and maintaining readability and scalability.

