### Advanced Web Development with Node.js and Express.js
In this project, you will build a full-stack web application using Node.js and Express.js. The application will allow users to create, edit, and delete posts, as well as view the most recent posts created by the site. You will also have the ability to comment on posts, like them, and see who liked them.

The following are the requirements for this project:
* Create a new Node.js application using Express.js.
* Set up the database for your application using MongoDB.
* Define routes for your application using Express.js.
* Use templates to render HTML views from your routes.
* Implement authentication for your application using Passport.js.
* Implement authorization for your application using Passport.js and JWT.
* Implement data validation in your application using Joi.
* Test your application using Postman or a similar tool.

### Project Structure
The project structure should follow the following layout:
```
- root
    - app
        - controllers
            - postController.js
        - models
            - postModel.js
        - routes
            - postRoutes.js
        - views
            - index.ejs
        - app.js
        - package.json
    - public
    - node_modules
```
### Controllers
In this project, we will create a `postController.js` file that will handle all the business logic for our application. This includes creating, updating and deleting posts as well as retrieving them from the database.
```
// postController.js
const Post = require('../models/postModel');

module.exports = {
    createPost: (req, res) => {
        const title = req.body.title;
        const content = req.body.content;

        if (!title || !content) {
            return res.status(400).json({ message: 'Please provide all fields' });
        }

        const post = new Post({ title, content });

        post.save()
            .then(() => res.json(post))
            .catch(err => console.log(err));
    },
    getPosts: (req, res) => {
        Post.find()
            .sort({ date: -1 })
            .then(posts => res.json(posts))
            .catch(err => console.log(err));
    },
    getPost: (req, res) => {
        const id = req.params.id;

        Post.findById(id)
            .then(post => res.json(post))
            .catch(err => console.log(err));
    },
    updatePost: (req, res) => {
        const id = req.params.id;
        const title = req.body.title;
        const content = req.body.content;

        if (!title || !content) {
            return res.status(400).json({ message: 'Please provide all fields' });
        }

        Post.findByIdAndUpdate(id, { title, content }, { new: true })
            .then(post => res.json(post))
            .catch(err => console.log(err));
    },
    deletePost: (req, res) => {
        const id = req.params.id;

        Post.findByIdAndRemove(id)
            .then(() => res.json({ message: 'Post deleted successfully' }))
            .catch(err => console.log(err));
    },
}
