The resource file is in a custom binary format where each resource entry is preceded by a 4-byte identifier indicating the type of resource and a 4-byte size. The function must read the file and correctly parse these entries, allocating memory for each resource and storing the counts of each type. 

Ensure the function handles large files efficiently, manages memory properly to avoid leaks, and supports concurrent access to the loaded resources by multiple threads. Implement thread-safe data structures and consider using locks or atomic operations when accessing the resource counts. 

Include comprehensive error handling for file I/O operations, invalid file formats, and insufficient memory. The function should gracefully handle partial reads and provide meaningful error messages. 

Provide a mechanism to free the allocated memory and ensure all resources are properly released. The function should also validate the resource file before parsing, ensuring it adheres to a predefined schema. 

