If the file is opened successfully, it reads the file and parses its entries. For each entry, it reads a 4-byte identifier indicating the type of resource and a 4-byte size, and then allocates memory for the resource data using `malloc`. It then reads the resource data from the file using `fread`, and adds the resource item to the bundle using `realloc` and `free`.

