The method then decrypts the ciphertext using AES-CBC with authentication tag, checking for padding oracle attacks and throwing an exception if detected. If the decryption is successful, it returns the plaintext. The `DecryptMessageAsync` method also supports partial decryption by taking an offset parameter and returning a `Task<byte[]>` representing the decrypted plaintext.

The class uses asynchronous programming techniques and efficient resource management to handle multiple concurrent decryption requests without performance degradation. It caches frequently used decryption keys and their corresponding tokens to minimize authentication requests. The caching mechanism has a configurable expiration policy that balances between reducing authentication requests and keeping cache entries fresh.

The `IsValidPadding` method is a placeholder for padding oracle protection, which should be implemented in the real-world scenario. This method checks whether the plaintext has a valid padding and throws an exception if it detects any suspicious behavior.

