The function also uses the `SyncLazy` module to install an ice hook that captures any errors that occur during compilation, and the `early_error` function to report these errors using the `println!` macro. The function also implements a mechanism to parallelize the compilation process to improve performance and efficiency, while ensuring that the number of concurrent compilations does not exceed a predefined threshold to manage system load.

