The `extract_and_cache_elements` function takes in an HTML document as input and returns a list of elements that match the given tag, attribute selector, and value. It first checks if the input parameters are valid and raises an exception if they are not. If the input is valid, it creates an instance of `ElementExtractor` and calls its `extract` method to perform the element extraction. The function returns the result from `ElementExtractor.extract`.

The code also includes logging for tracking cache hits and misses and provides a way to clear the cache manually. It also handles different character encodings in the HTML document, including UTF-8, ISO-8859-1, and GBK. Finally, it implements a unit test suite to verify the correctness and performance of the function under various conditions.

