```c++
class OctreeSpatialPartitioner {
private:
    // Data structure for storing spatial data points
    struct SpatialDataPoint {
        float x, y, z;
        int id;
    };

    // Octree node data structure
    struct OctreeNode {
        float minX, maxX, minY, maxY, minZ, maxZ;
        std::vector<SpatialDataPoint> points;
        OctreeNode* parent;
        OctreeNode* children[8];
    };

    // Root node of the octree
    OctreeNode root;

    // Current number of leaf nodes in the octree
    int numLeafNodes = 0;

    // Total capacity of the octree (in bytes)
    size_t totalCapacity = 0;

    // Minimum allowed memory usage (in bytes)
    const float minMemoryUsage = 1.0f;

    // Maximum allowed memory usage (in bytes)
    const float maxMemoryUsage = 1024.0f * 1024.0f * 1024.0f; // 1 GB

public:
    OctreeSpatialPartitioner() {
        root.minX = -FLT_MAX;
        root.maxX = FLT_MAX;
        root.minY = -FLT_MAX;
        root.maxY = FLT_MAX;
        root.minZ = -FLT_MAX;
        root.maxZ = FLT_MAX;
    }

    // Initialize the octree with a given capacity (in bytes)
    void init(size_t capacity) {
        if (capacity == 0 || capacity < minMemoryUsage) {
            throw std::invalid_argument("Invalid capacity");
        }
        totalCapacity = capacity;
        numLeafNodes = 0;
    }

    // Add a spatial data point to the octree
    void addDataPoint(float x, float y, float z) {
        if (totalCapacity == 0 || numLeafNodes >= totalCapacity / sizeof(SpatialDataPoint)) {
            throw std::runtime_error("Memory limit reached");
        }
        SpatialDataPoint point = {x, y, z};
        addNode(root, &point);
    }

    // Add a node to the octree
    void addNode(OctreeNode& node, SpatialDataPoint* point) {
        if (node.points.size() == 0 || numLeafNodes >= totalCapacity / sizeof(SpatialDataPoint)) {
            throw std::runtime_error("Memory limit reached");
        }
        node.points.push_back(*point);
        ++numLeafNodes;
    }

    // Query spatial data points within a given radius of a given point
    void query(float x, float y, float z, float radius) {
        std::vector<SpatialDataPoint> results;
        queryNode(root, x, y, z, radius, results);
        for (const SpatialDataPoint& result : results) {
            // Process the result
        }
    }

    // Query a node within a given radius of a given point
    void queryNode(OctreeNode& node, float x, float y, float z, float radius) {
        if (node.minX <= x && x <= node.maxX && node.minY <= y && y <= node.maxY && node.minZ <= z && z <= node.maxZ) {
            // This node contains the point
            for (const SpatialDataPoint& point : node.points) {
                float distance = sqrt((point.x - x) * (point.x - x) + (point.y - y) * (point.y - y) + (point.z - z) * (point.z - z));
                if (distance <= radius) {
                    // This point is within the radius
                    results.push_back(point);
                }
            }
        } else {
            // The node does not contain the point, query child nodes recursively
            for (int i = 0; i < 8; ++i) {
                if (node.children[i] != nullptr) {
                    queryNode(*node.children[i], x, y, z, radius);
                }
            }
        }
    }
};
```
The `OctreeSpatialPartitioner` class has the following methods:

* `init`: Initializes the octree with a given capacity (in bytes).
* `addDataPoint`: Adds a spatial data point to the octree.
* `query`: Queries spatial data points within a given radius of a given point.
* `queryNode`: Queries a node within a given radius of a given point.

The class also has several private methods that are used internally:

* `addNode`: Adds a node to the octree.
* `queryNode`: Recursively queries child nodes within a given radius of a given point.

The `SpatialDataPoint` struct is used to store spatial data points, with `x`, `y`, and `z` coordinates and an `id`. The `OctreeNode` struct is used to store octree nodes, with `minX`, `maxX`, `minY`, `maxY`, `minZ`, and `maxZ` bounds and a vector of `SpatialDataPoint`s.

The class has several member variables:

* `root`: The root node of the octree.
* `numLeafNodes`: The current number of leaf nodes in the octree.
* `totalCapacity`: The total capacity of the octree (in bytes).
* `minMemoryUsage`: The minimum allowed memory usage (in bytes) for the octree.
* `maxMemoryUsage`: The maximum allowed memory usage (in bytes) for the octree.

The class also has several private methods that are used internally:

* `addNode`: Adds a node to the octree.
* `queryNode`: Recursively queries child nodes within a given radius of a given point.

The `init` method initializes the octree with a given capacity (in bytes). If the capacity is invalid or less than the minimum allowed memory usage, an exception is thrown. Otherwise, the total capacity and number of leaf nodes are set to zero.

The `addDataPoint` method adds a spatial data point to the octree. If the total capacity of the octree has been reached or the number of leaf nodes exceeds the maximum allowed memory usage, an exception is thrown. Otherwise, the spatial data point is added to the appropriate node in the octree.

The `query` method queries spatial data points within a given radius of a given point. The method starts by querying the root node and then recursively queries child nodes until a matching result is found or all possible results have been exhausted. If no results are found, an empty vector is returned.

The `queryNode` method queries a node within a given radius of a given point. The method checks if the node contains the point and returns all spatial data points that are within the radius if it does. Otherwise, the method recursively queries child nodes until a matching result is found or all possible results have been exhausted. If no results are found, an empty vector is returned.

Here is an example of how to use the `OctreeSpatialPartitioner` class:
```
int main() {
    // Initialize the octree with a capacity of 10 MB
    OctreeSpatialPartitioner partitioner(10 * 1024 * 1024);

    // Add spatial data points to the octree
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; ++i) {
        partitioner.addDataPoint(i, i * 0.5f, i * 0.25f, i + 0.5f);
    }

    // Query spatial data points within a given radius of a given point
    std::vector<SpatialDataPoint> results;
    partitioner.query(10.0f, 10.0f, 10.0f, 5.0f, results);

    // Process the results
    for (const SpatialDataPoint& result : results) {
        std::cout << "Spatial data point found: x=" << result.x << ", y=" << result.y << ", z=" << result.z << std::endl;
    }

    return 0;
}
```
