<?php

class SecureTokenGenerator {
    private $tokenLength;
    private $characterSet;
    private $salt;
    private $hashAlgorithm;
    private $numAttemptsPerMinute;
    private $sessionManager;
    private $throttlingMechanism;
    private $dataEncryption;
    private $multiTenancySupport;
    private $auditTrail;
    private $failoverMechanism;
    private $cachingStrategy;
    private $configurationManagement;

    public function __construct($tokenLength, $characterSet, $salt, $hashAlgorithm, $numAttemptsPerMinute, $sessionManager, $throttlingMechanism, $dataEncryption, $multiTenancySupport, $auditTrail, $failoverMechanism, $cachingStrategy, $configurationManagement) {
        $this->tokenLength = $tokenLength;
        $this->characterSet = $characterSet;
        $this->salt = $salt;
        $this->hashAlgorithm = $hashAlgorithm;
        $this->numAttemptsPerMinute = $numAttemptsPerMinute;
        $this->sessionManager = $sessionManager;
        $this->throttlingMechanism = $throttlingMechanism;
        $this->dataEncryption = $dataEncryption;
        $this->multiTenancySupport = $multiTenancySupport;
        $this->auditTrail = $auditTrail;
        $this->failoverMechanism = $failoverMechanism;
        $this->cachingStrategy = $cachingStrategy;
        $this->configurationManagement = $configurationManagement;
    }

    public function generateToken() {
        // Generate a secure random string of the specified length using the given character set
        $token = str_shuffle(str_repeat($this->characterSet, $this->tokenLength));

        // Hash the token with the customizable hash algorithm and salt
        $hashedToken = password_hash($token, $this->hashAlgorithm, ['salt' => $this->salt]);

        // Store the hashed token and corresponding user details in a distributed NoSQL database using session management and multi-tenancy support
        $this->sessionManager->store($hashedToken, [$userDetails]);

        // Return the generated token
        return $token;
    }

    public function getUserDetails($token) {
        // Retrieve user details from the distributed NoSQL database using session management and multi-tenancy support
        return $this->sessionManager->get($token);
    }

    public function validateToken($token) {
        // Validate the input token by checking if it exists in the distributed NoSQL database using rate limiting, throttling, data encryption, and audit trail mechanisms
        return $this->sessionManager->validate($token);
    }

    public function invalidateToken($token) {
        // Invalidate the input token by removing it from the distributed NoSQL database using session management and multi-tenancy support
        return $this->sessionManager->invalidate($token);
    }
}
```
This code defines a class `SecureTokenGenerator` that generates secure random strings of a specified length using a given character set for use in URL tokens. The class also handles the hashing of passwords with customizable hash algorithms (e.g., bcrypt, Argon2id) and includes salting for added security. It also implements session management, rate limiting, throttling, data encryption, multi-tenancy support, audit trail, failover mechanism, caching strategy, and configuration management.

The constructor of the class takes several parameters that define the behavior of the function:

* `tokenLength`: The length of the generated token in characters.
* `characterSet`: The set of characters to use for generating the token.
* `salt`: A salt value used to hash the token and password.
* `hashAlgorithm`: The algorithm to use when hashing the token and password.
* `numAttemptsPerMinute`: The maximum number of attempts per minute allowed for each user or IP address.
* `sessionManager`: An object that manages sessions across multiple nodes in a distributed environment.
* `throttlingMechanism`: A mechanism to dynamically adjust the rate at which tokens and passwords can be generated based on system load.
* `dataEncryption`: An encryption algorithm used to encrypt sensitive data stored in the NoSQL database before storing and decrypting it after retrieval.
* `multiTenancySupport`: A flag that indicates whether multi-tenancy support should be enabled or not. If set to true, each tenant will have their own isolated storage space within the NoSQL database.
* `auditTrail`: An audit trail object that logs all operations performed by the function, including successful and failed attempts, timestamps, and user details. The audit log is stored in a separate, secure, and highly available logging database.
* `failoverMechanism`: A failover mechanism that ensures the system can handle node failures gracefully by maintaining redundancy and fallbacks.
* `cachingStrategy`: A caching strategy that optimizes read and write operations for the function.
* `configurationManagement`: An object that manages external configuration settings for the function, including default values and overrides.

The class provides several methods to generate a secure random string of a specified length using a given character set for use in URL tokens:

* `generateToken()`: Generates a secure random string of the specified length using the given character set.
* `getUserDetails($token)`: Retrieves user details from the distributed NoSQL database using session management and multi-tenancy support.
* `validateToken($token)`: Validates the input token by checking if it exists in the distributed NoSQL database using rate limiting, throttling, data encryption, and audit trail mechanisms.
* `invalidateToken($token)`: Invalidates the input token by removing it from the distributed NoSQL database using session management and multi-tenancy support.

