  private boolean running;

  public ServiceManager() {
    this.executor = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();
    this.running = false;
  }

  public void start() {
    if (this.running) {
      return;
    }
    this.running = true;
    this.executor.scheduleAtFixedRate(this::sendHeartbeat, HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL, HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
  }

  public void stop() {
    if (!this.running) {
      return;
    }
    this.running = false;
    this.executor.shutdown();
  }

  private void sendHeartbeat() {
    try {
      // Send heartbeat message to remote monitoring system
      HttpResponse response = HttpUtils.sendRequest("POST", LOGGING_ENDPOINT, HEARTBEAT_MESSAGE);
      if (response.getStatusCode() != 200) {
        System.out.println("Heartbeat message was not received");
        return;
      }
      // Fetch configuration from external API and update service state
      response = HttpUtils.sendRequest("GET", API_ENDPOINT);
      if (response.getStatusCode() != 200) {
        System.out.println("Failed to fetch configuration");
        return;
      }
      // Process configuration updates and handle errors
      try {
        JSONObject config = new JSONObject(response.getBody());
        this.updateServiceState(config);
      } catch (JSONException e) {
        System.out.println("Failed to parse configuration: " + e.getMessage());
        return;
      }
    } catch (IOException e) {
      System.out.println("Network error while sending heartbeat");
    }
  }

  private void updateServiceState(JSONObject config) {
    // Update service state based on configuration updates
  }

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    ServiceManager manager = new ServiceManager();
    manager.start();
  }
}
```
This code creates a single-threaded executor to schedule the heartbeat message sending task at regular intervals using `scheduleAtFixedRate()` method. The `running` flag is used to track whether the service is currently running or not. The `sendHeartbeat()` method sends a heartbeat message to the remote monitoring system and fetches the configuration from an external API using `HttpUtils` library. If there are any errors while processing the configuration updates, the method catches the exceptions and logs them.

