The `processPayment` method validates the inputs, handles different payment gateways by delegating the actual processing logic to respective gateway classes, and implements retry logic in case of failures or timeouts during payment processing. It returns a status message indicating success, failure, or pending.

The `refundPayment` method first validates the input parameters, queries the transaction details for the given order using the payment gateway, calculates the refund amount, and initiates the refund process using the same gateway. It also handles partial refunds and logs all refund attempts for auditing purposes.

The `createOrder` method first validates the input parameters, inserts a new order into the database, and returns the generated order ID. It also implements caching for frequently accessed customer information to optimize database queries for better performance.

