The `IsValidUserId` method is used to validate the input data, and it should be implemented according to your specific requirements. In this example, we have just returned `true` for any valid user ID, but you may want to implement more sophisticated validation logic to ensure that the user IDs are in a valid format and correspond to actual users in your system.

The `FetchProfileAsync` method is used to fetch profiles from the API and cache them. It first retrieves profiles from the cache using Redis, then fetches missing profiles from the API and caches them. If all attempts to retrieve a profile fail, it logs an error message and returns `null`.

The `UserProfileCache` class also has a constructor that accepts parameters for the Redis connection multiplexer, HTTP client, API URL, and cache expiration time. The constructor initializes the `_userIds` field with an empty list of user IDs, which is used to keep track of the input user IDs.

