This code generates a random value within the specified range, both inclusively and exclusively, supporting floating-point and integer types. The `CustomRange` method takes two parameters: a minimum value, `min`, and a maximum value, `max`. It also takes a third parameter, `rangeType`, of type `RangeType`, which specifies the range type (either inclusive, exclusive, or half-open). The `SeedManager` class handles seeding and synchronization for multiple threads, with automatic reseeding to prevent long-term bias. The class also includes a mechanism for integration with external systems, allowing customization of the random number generation logic using a callback function for when a new seed is generated. Finally, this code includes robust error handling, including validation of input parameters and exception handling for invalid range inputs.

