Here is a sample C++ program implementing a multi-threaded random number generator service using the Mersenne Twister algorithm:
```c++
#include <iostream>
#include <random>
#include <mutex>
#include <thread>
#include <vector>
#include <cstdlib>

namespace RandomService {
    class ThreadSafeGenerator {
        private:
            std::mt19937 mt; // Mersenne Twister generator
            std::mutex mtx; // Mutex for thread-safe access to the generator
            int seed; // Unique seed for each thread

        public:
            ThreadSafeGenerator() {
                seed = SeedFromThreadID();
                mt.seed(seed);
            }

            ~ThreadSafeGenerator() {
                // Clean up any resources used by the generator
            }

            static int SeedFromThreadID() {
                std::stringstream ss;
                ss << std::this_thread::get_id();
                return std::stoi(ss.str());
            }

            int getRandomNumber() {
                mtx.lock(); // Lock the mutex to ensure thread-safe access to the generator
                int random = mt();
                mtx.unlock();
                return random;
            }
    };
}

int main() {
    std::vector<std::thread> threads;
    for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {
        threads.push_back(std::thread([](RandomService::ThreadSafeGenerator *generator) {
            int randomNumber = generator->getRandomNumber();
            std::cout << "Generated random number: " << randomNumber << std::endl;
        }, new RandomService::ThreadSafeGenerator()));
    }
    for (auto &t : threads) {
        t.join();
    }
    return 0;
}
```
This program defines a `ThreadSafeGenerator` class within the `RandomService` namespace that provides thread-safe random number generation using the Mersenne Twister algorithm. The class has a constructor that initializes the generator with a unique seed derived from the thread ID, and a destructor that cleans up any resources used by the generator.

The program also includes a static member function `SeedFromThreadID` that returns the unique seed value for each thread. This function uses the `std::this_thread::get_id()` function to get the current thread ID, and converts it to a string using an `std::stringstream`. The resulting string is then converted back to an integer using the `std::stoi` function to generate a unique seed for each thread.

The `getRandomNumber()` member function of the `ThreadSafeGenerator` class uses the mutex `mtx` to ensure that only one thread can access the generator at a time, and generates a random number using the `mt()` function of the Mersenne Twister algorithm. The generated random number is then returned to the caller.

The program also includes a `main()` function that creates ten threads, each with its own instance of the `ThreadSafeGenerator`. Each thread calls the `getRandomNumber()` member function to generate a random number, and prints it to the console using `std::cout`. The threads are joined after they have completed their execution.

