The `UploadFileAsync` method takes a file path and a bucket name as input parameters, validates them, and then creates a new blob client for the input file using the specified bucket name. The method then uploads the file to the cloud storage provider using the `UploadAsync` method provided by the Azure Blob Storage SDK. If an error occurs during the upload process, the method returns an instance of the `UploadResult` class with a success status of `false` and detailed error information.

The `UploadBytesAsync` method is similar to the `UploadFileAsync` method but takes a byte array as input instead of a file path. The method validates the input parameters, creates a new blob client for the input byte array using the specified bucket name, and then uploads the byte array to the cloud storage provider using the `UploadAsync` method provided by the Azure Blob Storage SDK.

The `DownloadFileAsync` method takes a file path and a bucket name as input parameters, validates them, creates a new blob client for the input file using the specified bucket name, and then downloads the file from the cloud storage provider using the `DownloadToAsync` method provided by the Azure Blob Storage SDK.

The `DownloadBytesAsync` method is similar to the `DownloadFileAsync` method but takes a bucket name and an optional blob name as input parameters instead of a file path. The method validates the input parameters, creates a new blob client for the input byte array using the specified bucket name and blob name, and then downloads the byte array from the cloud storage provider using the `OpenReadAsync` method provided by the Azure Blob Storage SDK.

