The `extractOAuthToken()` method extracts the OAuth token from the authorization header of the incoming request. It checks if the header is valid and contains an OAuth token by matching the `^Bearer\s+(.*)$` pattern against the header value. If the token is found, it returns the token.

The `isValidOAuthToken()` method checks if the given token is valid by loading the user entity from the database using the token and checking if the token exists in the database. It returns true if the token is valid, false otherwise.

The `onAuthenticationSuccess()` method is called when authentication is successful. It loads the user entity from the database using the OAuth token, creates a new Symfony security token with the user entity and adds it to the request.

The `onAuthenticationFailure()` method is called when authentication fails. It returns a 401 response with an error message if the authentication fails.

